{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"stational-oppressed-apatosaur","creation_channel":"python","description":"Store only the SET of Jira keys seen last pass instead of the full ACLI payload. prev_snapshot is\n**228.1 MB / 4.5 MB per day** — the largest term after A1. session_log **1cb6-d553-6565-49b4** (measured facts; do not re-derive).\n\n## Measured effect\nOver the newest **400 real revisions**: **218 of 399** consecutive pairs have an **identical key\nset** (so they become byte-identical and produce no commit at all), and when it changes the mean\nsymmetric difference is **1.78 keys**. Key-set payload at HEAD is **19,960 bytes** vs a **27.1 MB**\nfull payload.\n\n## Why this is safe — gate G1 was cleared empirically, not by reasoning\nA corpus mutation-diff ran the real differ over **four real snapshot pairs** with full prev vs\nkey-set prev and found **zero difference in any mutation reaching Jira with a non-empty effect**.\nThe feared `_compute_mutations_emit_both` field-clearing does not reach Jira:\n`_mutation_to_batch_dict` reads `payload[\"changed_fields\"]` for updates, which branch-3 never sets,\nso `fields` collapses to `{}` and `update_issue(key)` short-circuits at `acli.py:181-185` with zero\nsubprocess and zero network.\n\n**It also removes a latent bug.** With today's full prev, keys in prev-but-not-curr emit\n`(outbound, create)` carrying the departed issue's raw field blob — and that payload shape DOES reach\n`create_one`. Corpus: **973-998 spurious Jira creates** whenever the fetch window shrinks or the\nproject is re-targeted. A key-set emits none.\n\nShape constraint: store a **dict** `{jira_key: {}}`, not a `set` — `check_dual_identity_complete`\nand `_emit_both`'s `local_state[key] or {}` guards assume dict entries.\n\n## Rollback (mandatory artifact)\nThe G1 corpus diff ran **forward only**. Before merging, run it **backward** (key-set -> full, the\nrevert direction) and record the result. Deleting `prev_snapshot.json` is **not** a safe default\nescape hatch: an empty prev is exactly what made the differ re-derive 2050+ inbound creates every\npass (`reconcile.py:258-259`), because `differ.py:455-490` emits an inbound CREATE for every\ncurr-only key unless a `rebar-id:` label suppresses it — bound pairs are safe, unbound in-window keys\nare not. If deletion is ever used, it MUST be followed by a cap-0/no-write pass proving zero inbound\ncreates.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Corpus mutation-diff (full prev vs key-set prev) over **>=4 real snapshot pairs** shows **zero\n      difference** in any mutation reaching Jira with a non-empty effect. Tier: **repo-level corpus\n      script** committed under the experiments path.\n- [ ] The **reverse-direction** diff (key-set -> full) is recorded on this ticket as the rollback\n      artifact, showing the revert path emits no unexpected inbound creates. Tier: **repo-level\n      corpus script**.\n- [ ] Branch-2 regression is gone: with a key-set prev and >=900 prev-only keys, **zero**\n      `(outbound, create)` mutations are emitted. Tier: **unit** on `compute_mutations`.\n- [ ] `check_dual_identity_complete` and the binding-walk adopt-skip set behave identically with\n      `{}` entries. Tier: **unit**.\n- [ ] prev_snapshot at HEAD is <=64 KB after one pass. Verify: byte measurement.\n\n## Files\n`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile.py` (prev persist),\n`run_differs.py`, tests, corpus script\n\nScope: M. Depends on A4-1.","id":"b197-ad42-d931-4ba0","parent_id":"96bc-3004-3d7f-4da5","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"A4-2: narrow prev_snapshot.json to a bare key-set {jira_key: {}}"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788216296926892001,"uuid":"b9aec237-d515-4e48-89bd-fdd807b5e4af"}